      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(config): warn when JSON5 comments are lost on config write",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw uses JSON5 to parse user configurations (supporting comments), but writes them back with JSON.stringify which silently strips all user-authored comments on every automatic config write.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTwo issues fixed:\n1. JSON5.parse discards comments — they cannot survive the parse-modify-stringify roundtrip\n2. The initial regex had a URL false positive (`http://...`) and missed inline block comments\n\nThe fix strips string literals before checking for comment markers, so URLs inside strings don't trigger warnings while real comments (including inline `/* */`) are still detected.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Users with JSON5 comments in config now see a warning before their comments are stripped\n- URLs inside strings (`http://...`) do not cause false warnings\n- Inline block comments (`{a: 1 /* note */}`) are correctly detected\n- Plain JSON configs produce no warning\n\n## Evidence\n\n```\n$ node -e\n\n✅ \"// comment\"                     → true  — line-start comment\n✅ \"  // indented\"                  → true  — indented comment\n✅ \"/* block */\"                    → true  — block comment\n✅ \"\\\"http://url\\\"\"                 → false — URL in string (no false positive)\n✅ \"\\\"// not a comment\\\"\"           → false — // in string value\n✅ \"plain json\"                     → false — plain JSON\n✅ \"{a: 1 /* inline */}\"            → true  — inline block comment (outside string)\n✅ \"\\\"/* in string */\\\"\"           → false — /* in string value\n\nResult: 8/8 passed\n```\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/config/schema.test.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  59 passed (59)\n\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/config/io.owner-display-secret.test.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  2 passed (2)\n```\n\n```\n$ npx oxlint -c .oxlintrc.json src/config/io.ts\n  No errors\n\n$ npx oxfmt --check src/config/io.ts\n  All matched files use the correct format\n```\n\n## What Changed\n\n- src/config/io.ts: +18 lines (string-aware `hasJSON5Comments()` helper + warning)\n\nFixes #105683\n\n## AI Assistance 🤖\n- **AI-assisted**: Yes\n- **Co-Authored-By**: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n- **Human confirmed understanding**: Yes",
